EPIC-260715-3810we_tcp-dns-system-vpn/STORY-260715-eto58m_vpn-manager-and-extension-lifecycle/TASK-260715-3lab1f_add-vpn-manager-and-provider-lifecycle-tests/README.md:7:In scope: unrelated manager fixtures, save or reload conflicts, permission and invalid states, connect and disconnect races, provider start failures, app-message versions, app recreation, stop reasons, completion once, repeated lifecycle loops, and resource baselines. Out of scope: physical system permission dialogs, final UI tests, packet throughput, DNS leak capture, reconnect, UDP, TestFlight, and notarization.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/README.md:1:# M5 — Release and distribution
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-3e7noa_pin-relay-release-build-environments-and-inputs/README.md:7:In scope: relay source and generated protocol revision, HEV or other native dependency pins used by the relay, package locks, container image digests, macOS Xcode or SDK identity, cross toolchains and sysroots, checksum-verified downloads, offline or post-fetch builds, locale and timezone, path remapping, compiler flags, and input inventory. Out of scope: building final assets, changing dependency choices without a decision, Apple application dependencies not shipped with relay, and storing credentials in images or locks.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-3e7noa_pin-relay-release-build-environments-and-inputs/README.md:10:1. Every source, dependency, generator, toolchain, image, SDK, sysroot, and downloaded archive is addressed by immutable revision and cryptographic digest where supported. 2. A clean bootstrap verifies all digests before use and the actual build can run without resolving mutable branches, tags, latest URLs, or undeclared network inputs. 3. Environment, locale, timezone, paths, compiler flags, linker flags, archive ordering, and build metadata are normalized per the reproducibility contract. 4. The input inventory records licenses and provenance and contains no access tokens, private registry credentials, developer home paths, or private key material. 5. Controlled pin, digest, lock, image, SDK, flag, and undeclared-fetch drift fails before compilation.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-3kepzm_verify-independent-relay-build-reproducibility/README.md:10:1. Two isolated builds for each of the four targets use the same approved input digest set and produce identical unsigned SHA-256 values. 2. The verification proves caches and prior outputs cannot satisfy either build and records runner or container, toolchain, SDK, locale, time, and command identity. 3. Any mismatch produces bounded diagnostics identifying differing sections or metadata without uploading source secrets or entire proprietary environments. 4. Known deterministic-normalization steps are tested independently and no post-build byte patch can conceal a source or toolchain difference. 5. A mismatch blocks manifest generation and release staging until the input or nondeterminism is fixed and the full pair is rerun.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-pa6evr_record-relay-release-input-and-reproducibility-contract/README.md:7:In scope: approved source revisions, submodules or vendored inputs, lockfiles, compiler and linker versions, container or runner images, Linux and macOS x86_64 and arm64 targets, environment normalization, timestamps, paths, locale, archive order, build identity, output names, bit-for-bit pass condition, manifest schema, SBOM format, license policy, vulnerability thresholds, provenance predicate, and exception approval. Out of scope: implementing builds, changing relay protocol behavior, Apple signing, remote installation, and silently classifying unexplained differences as acceptable.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-243sh0_ios-testflight-and-app-store/TASK-260715-1bni66_validate-app-store-binary-technical-preflight/README.md:7:In scope: exact App Store Connect build ID, local archive or export digest, validation transport, bundle and app-record mapping, versions, profiles and entitlements, architecture, privacy manifests, required-reason APIs, symbols, encryption inventory, prohibited content or private APIs, server warnings, build selection lock, and evidence handoff to the review package. Out of scope: final privacy or export declarations, age rating, content rights, public metadata, screenshots, support and privacy URLs, storefront approval, App Review submission, and dismissing Apple warnings without an owned disposition.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/README.md:7:In scope: release version manifest and go or no-go control, role separation and approvals, cross-platform release and rollback runbooks, current Apple guidance revalidation, public privacy policy and in-app parity, App Privacy labels, export-compliance and regional VPN licensing or storefront decisions, support and retention statements, App Review data-flow and entitlement-purpose evidence, degraded-mode and system-exclusion disclosure, user-owned SSH exit explanation, non-production review host or reproducible setup, review account or profile handling, metadata and screenshot evidence, release-candidate matrix, behavior-to-claim traceability, submission, response handling, incident and credential revocation, and durable audit evidence. Out of scope: inventing legal advice, changing product behavior to match unsupported claims, sharing production credentials, launching unsupported regions, implementing tunnel features, or bypassing negative Gate A0, P0, signing, TestFlight, privacy, or regression evidence.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/README.md:10:1. A versioned release manifest and runbook identify candidate commits and artifacts, owners, approvals, required CI gates, promotion order, communication, retention, abort criteria, rollback, revocation, and post-release checks for relay, macOS, and iOS. 2. A currently dated primary-source review plus accountable product, privacy, legal, security, and regional approvals produce public policy, App Privacy labels, export-compliance answers, retention or deletion commitments, and storefront availability that match actual behavior. 3. The App Review package accurately explains the VPN data path, Network Extension purpose, user-owned SSH exit, observer boundaries, system exclusions, full and degraded modes, diagnostics, support data, and regional limits without claiming anonymity or a Relux-operated exit service. 4. Reviewers receive a reproducible test profile or isolated SSH host and instructions that exercise the submitted binary without exposing private production credentials; access is scoped, monitored for abuse, rotated, and removed after review. 5. The exact signed candidates pass the supported simulator, physical iPhone, Apple-silicon Mac, accessibility, privacy, leak, lifecycle, entitlement, notarization, TestFlight, artifact, migration, install, upgrade, and rollback matrix, with failures blocking promotion. 6. Submission metadata, screenshots, privacy and support URLs, binary and build identifiers, reviewer notes, communications, rejections, corrections, and resubmissions are preserved and traceable to the reviewed behavior and evidence revision.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/TASK-260715-2dxzjv_author-reproducible-app-review-test-instructions/README.md:7:In scope: exact build ID and version, supported device and OS, review account or profile fields, secure credential delivery references, hostname and fingerprint, expected host-trust UI, privacy disclosure, permission prompts, connect and disconnect, external IP or DNS evidence using safe destinations, UDP and degraded demonstration, system exclusions and limitations, diagnostics and support export, background and relaunch, error recovery, screenshots, time estimate, support contact, fixture health fallback, and teardown. Out of scope: asking reviewers to disable host verification, use production secrets, install development tooling, infer undocumented behavior, bypass system security, or rely on private company network access.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/TASK-260715-2dxzjv_author-reproducible-app-review-test-instructions/README.md:10:1. A reviewer starting from a clean supported physical iPhone can complete the primary flow using only the submitted build, approved secure credentials, public policy and support URLs, and the instructions. 2. Every field, button, prompt, expected state, delay, system permission, full or degraded result, error recovery, and cleanup step matches the exact candidate and current screenshots. 3. Host-key verification is explicit, changed-key behavior is explained, and no step uses silent acceptance, agent forwarding, shell access, or production credentials. 4. Instructions accurately disclose the user-owned SSH model, exit-host visibility, system exclusions, compatible or fail-closed behavior, diagnostics boundaries, and no Relux-operated exit service. 5. An independent clean-device rehearsal records duration, build ID, fixture revision, screenshots, ambiguities, failure recovery, and corrections and the final instructions contain no secrets outside the approved secure credential fields.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/TASK-260715-3cg87m_revalidate-current-apple-review-privacy-export-and-vpn-requirements/README.md:7:In scope: official Apple Developer and App Store Connect sources, access dates and revisions, organization and VPN requirements, entitlement purpose, data-use and retention statements, privacy manifest and label rules, required-reason APIs, encryption questions, regional storefront controls, age rating and content rights, review credentials and notes, screenshots, support and privacy URLs, submission states, and revalidation triggers. Out of scope: relying on blogs as authority, legal advice, contacting Apple under Gate A0 unless required by its owner, product implementation, and treating point-in-time findings as permanent.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/TASK-260715-3rdsap_execute-cross-platform-release-candidate-regression-matrix/README.md:7:In scope: exact macOS DMG digest and App Store Connect iOS build ID, supported current and minimum Apple OS rows on named hardware, install and upgrade, host and extension signatures and entitlements, first run and disclosure, profile and host trust, full and degraded connection, TCP, DNS and UDP representative traffic, system exclusions, endpoint routing, network changes, sleep and wake, app termination, diagnostics and support export, accessibility, localization, migration or coexistence, uninstall, TestFlight withdrawal and macOS rollback evidence, resource metrics, and issue disposition. Out of scope: implementing fixes, simulator-only substitution for platform gates, production credentials or traffic, skipping unstable rows, and reusing earlier results from different bytes.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/TASK-260715-3rdsap_execute-cross-platform-release-candidate-regression-matrix/README.md:10:1. Every row starts from the exact remote candidate identifier and records device, OS, source, dependency revisions, relay manifest, configuration, duration, traffic shape, network conditions, memory, channels, associations, drops, errors, and artifact digest. 2. Signatures, entitlements, notarization, TestFlight install, extension lifecycle, full or degraded predicates, routing and DNS safety, diagnostics redaction, privacy gates, accessibility, migration, uninstall, and rollback all pass their declared criteria. 3. External IPv4, IPv6 where supported, and DNS observations match the intended exit and only documented Apple or endpoint exceptions use the physical path. 4. Failures create linked bugs with reproducible evidence and block promotion; reruns use a new evidence revision and cannot erase failed history. 5. A TASK-ID-scoped matrix summary gives pass or fail by row, exact candidate, artifact links, screenshots and captures after redaction, anomalies, residual risks, and release blockers.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-anxje6_continuous-integration-quality-gates/TASK-260728-1glezz_configure-autonomous-serial-agent-policy/progress.md:28:- [x] New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260717-1ecq74_macos-self-update/TASK-260717-rk4mi7_implement-update-settings-ui-and-background-scheduling/README.md:7:In scope: ReluxProxyMac host-only settings/presentation model; persisted non-secret preferences; Sparkle updater configuration and check-now command; injectable scheduler and updater seams; stable/pre-release channel policy only when metadata enables it; localizable English copy through the repository localization path; deterministic Swift Testing coverage for idle, checking, up-to-date, available, downloading, failed, schedule, relaunch, and disabled-automatic-check behavior; focused macOS build and tests. Out of scope: update installation, signed appcast generation/publication, private EdDSA material, Developer ID/notary ceremony, provider changes, system-extension activation, VPN connection, route/DNS changes, iOS, or physical update replacement validation.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260717-1ecq74_macos-self-update/TASK-260717-rk4mi7_implement-update-settings-ui-and-background-scheduling/README.md:10:1. The macOS host exposes non-focus-stealing menu-bar update settings for automatic checks, Check for Updates, and channel selection only when the configured feed policy enables pre-release updates. 2. Automatic-check and channel preferences persist across lifecycle reconstruction without storing secrets, and the accepted Sparkle controller receives the effective values through a narrow host-only adapter. 3. Check for Updates invokes the injected updater exactly once and background scheduling is deterministic, cancel-safe, idempotent, and suppressed when automatic checks are disabled. 4. A presentation model maps updater lifecycle events to idle/checking/up-to-date/available/downloading/failed states with localizable English copy and no raw URL, signature, key, path, or error-secret leakage. 5. Swift Testing covers persistence, channel gating, check-now, scheduling/cancellation/relaunch, every presentation state, and failure redaction; focused ReluxProxyMac tests and a host build pass without network installation or VPN/system-extension activation.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260717-1ecq74_macos-self-update/TASK-260717-rk4mi7_implement-update-settings-ui-and-background-scheduling/progress.md:22:- [x] Add localizable menu-bar settings controls without focus stealing
