EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2mtjdn_m4-product-decisions-and-validation/TASK-260715-zwtrhy_run-physical-m4-product-security-and-accessibility-matrix/README.md:10:1. On the named Apple-silicon Mac, with the iPhone row deferred with iOS under ADR-024, a user can configure, trust, acknowledge privacy, grant permission, connect, understand authoritative full/degraded/reasserting/failure state, inspect/export/delete diagnostics, and disconnect with system VPN status matching the provider. 2. Changed host key stops before auth; credentials remain in the approved Keychain boundary; app termination does not stop an active provider; diagnostics/export contain no prohibited markers. 3. Mac legacy behavior matches the approved coexist/migrate/retire decision with idempotency/rollback evidence and the preserved legacy build/release contract referenced. 4. VoiceOver plus keyboard complete the Mac journey, and the VoiceOver iPhone journey is recorded as deferred, at supported text scaling/contrast/motion settings with no critical accessibility blocker. 5. A TASK-ID-scoped redacted evidence bundle records matrix rows, environments, opaque fixture IDs, screenshots, system/capability state, export manifest/hash/categories, accessibility observations, cleanup, linked M1-M3 evidence, and explicit pass/fail.
