LOGBOOK.md:10:- DECISION: The macOS-first M0 Bridge gate passes under ADR-024 with MTU 1500, requested/effective 32768-byte socket buffers, 64-packet/5-ms pump budgets, HEV task-stack/TCP/UDP-copy values 24576/4096/2, and an initial measured 500-session ceiling. MTU 4096 remains injectable behind end-to-end proof; MTU 8500 is a named failed default candidate because constrained-buffer rows produced 768 `EMSGSIZE` refusals.
LOGBOOK.md:13:- GAPS: Physical iPhone, jetsam, NAT64, sleep/wake, energy, and whole-extension memory stay deferred/blocked and are never inferred from macOS. M1 consumers may use this baseline only through the exact accepted-outcome binding task; production composition remains fail-closed on its other M0 inputs.
LOGBOOK.md:34:- FIX: The physical-matrix entry now independently computes the actual working candidate tree with a task-local temporary Git index and rejects a well-formed forged `RELUX_CANDIDATE_TREE_OID` before HEV work or evidence emission. It independently hashes the linked macOS HEV archive against the pinned manifest. Negative production-call-site coverage rejects forged tree and artifact hashes.
LOGBOOK.md:39:- MEASUREMENT: A physical Mac15,9 (arm64, macOS 26.5) SwiftPM run admitted 100, 250, and the explicitly narrowed 500-session ceiling with zero bridge drops. Physical footprint was 12,354,160 B, 15,270,512 B, and 20,038,256 B; peak was 20,054,640 B. The incremental 500-session HEV/bridge cost was 11,976,704 B, leaving 19,480,576 B inside the provisional 30 MiB envelope. This is not a whole-extension Apple guarantee and does not allocate SSH, DNS, relay, caches, or reconnect overlap.
LOGBOOK.md:41:- AVAILABILITY: `os_proc_available_memory` is explicitly unavailable on macOS in the public SDK. HEV queued bytes and process-wide Swift task counts also have no public gauge. All are recorded as unavailable/unknown; host memory, process threads, and proxy zeros were not substituted. Physical iPhone and sleep/wake remain named deferred gaps.
LOGBOOK.md:46:### 2356 — Physical macOS MTU/socket baseline separates queue drops from send refusal (TASK-260715-gyg51r)
LOGBOOK.md:47:- MEASUREMENT: The bounded loopback-only SPM harness ran 36 rows on a physical Apple M3 Max Mac (arm64, macOS 26.5): MTU 1500/4096/8500 × IPv4/native IPv6/dual stack × nominal/constrained-buffer/25ms receiver-stall/mixed bidirectional traffic. Nominal and mixed rows delivered 100%; pressure rows produced only named bounded effects and recovered with zero production-owned descriptor delta. Swift-task delta is explicitly unavailable because the synchronous runner owns no tasks; process threads are not treated as a proxy.
LOGBOOK.md:51:- VERIFICATION: The full Swift suite passed 474 tests in 40 suites (25 declared known ReluxNIOSSH-unavailable issues); focused matrix coverage is 87.10% regions, 88.17% functions, and 96.13% lines. Strict affected-file format lint and diff checks pass. Raw and analyzed task evidence is attached on the board.
LOGBOOK.md:62:- VERIFICATION: Twenty-one focused Python tests include compiler/typechecker/preprocessor-backed regressions for all six re-review 04 bypasses plus the prior C macro, escaped-identifier, function-pointer, token-paste, Swift initializer/typealias, Objective-C selector, and Go import cases. The relay-toolchain CI job now checks out full Git history and has a static regression binding that setting to the provenance audit. Supply-chain/asset audits, manifest tests, relay Go tests/vet, unsigned Swift build, formatting/lint, privacy, diff, full-history local-clone audit, and byte-identical double generation are the handoff gates.
LOGBOOK.md:65:### 1035 — Relay assets bind exact source/build provenance to deferred M5 release controls (TASK-260715-vtot05)
LOGBOOK.md:67:- POLICY: M2 owns source pinning, reproducibility, asset hashes, and notices. Signing (`TASK-260715-3sk5cd`), notarization (`TASK-260715-387eof`), release attestation (`TASK-260715-1gzhnk`), and distribution approval (`TASK-260715-312u2k`) remain concrete M5 scopes; this task performs none of them.
LOGBOOK.md:72:- DOCUMENTATION: `docs/generated-workspace-foundation.md` is now the developer authority for clean checkout, pinned tools, generation, unsigned builds/tests, harness and relay smoke, four relay cross-builds, target ownership, non-secret Gate P0 inputs, dependency updates, artifact locations, troubleshooting, current validation limits, and legacy coexistence. `README.md` links the full gate and `CONTRIBUTING.md` now distinguishes the macOS 15/Swift tools 6.1 v2 baseline from legacy macOS 14/Swift 5.10.
LOGBOOK.md:73:- VERIFICATION: On revision `d18847cd6d7f3b84bdd807eddbca37d9259945de`, the exact `make credential-free-validate LEGACY_ROOT=/Users/iv/Developer/relux-proxy` gate exits 0 after checksum-pinned relay bootstrap. Relay packaging, deterministic generation, unsigned Debug/Release macOS targets, generated target contracts, all shared Swift tests, Release build, native packaging, detached legacy v0.1.0 preservation/guard/tests/Release build, focused harness suite, inline redacted harness smoke, diff checks, and board validation pass.
LOGBOOK.md:74:- FAIL-CLOSED FINDINGS: Before relay bootstrap, workspace/macOS/command-contract gates correctly exited 2/2/1 for the missing verified relay input. The first drafted harness example exited 64 because its profile reference was not an opaque UUID and was corrected to a synthetic UUID. Direct validation of the developer's independently evolving sibling legacy checkout exited 2, while the gate-owned detached v0.1.0 clone passed; clean-checkout docs now clone the tag explicitly.
LOGBOOK.md:75:- SAFETY: Production signing, physical Gate P0, Developer ID archive, notarization, DMG publication, iOS, installation, app/provider launch, VPN preference save/activation, route mutation, and DNS mutation were not run. Documentation makes no shipping claim and routes physical work only through dedicated-host gate `TASK-260819-25e1ys`.
LOGBOOK.md:78:- VERIFICATION: A fresh local `--no-hardlinks` clone of authoritative revision `7dc73ac6e7325f86a4a178a0558619f0fc9d1490` passed `make credential-free-validate` in 310.40 seconds. Evidence covers the exact six macOS-only workspace schemes, four generated targets, Debug/Release configurations, unsigned host/provider builds, deterministic double generation, static universal provider linkage, verified relay resources, 443 Swift tests, and detached legacy `v0.1.0` test/build. Product Swift coverage is 89.97% lines, 89.62% functions, and 82.11% regions; strict product Swift formatting and board validation pass.
LOGBOOK.md:79:- ARCHITECTURE: The Release provider is universal `arm64`/`x86_64`, embeds `ReluxTunnelMacOSAdapter` plus HEV/libssh2 production symbols, contains no `CReluxNativeFixture` or forbidden runtime-loader symbol, links only system frameworks/libraries, and embeds a checksum-valid four-platform relay payload. No signing overlay, embedded private-key payload, signing, installation, launch, VPN preference/tunnel, route, or DNS mutation was used.
LOGBOOK.md:83:- VERIFICATION: A detached no-hardlink clone of revision `409b3b4151c9f2f7bac7392595583b3fe971e455` passed the repository-owned credential-free matrix in 316.05 seconds: deterministic double generation, the exact six macOS-only schemes and four Xcode targets, unsigned Debug/Release host/provider builds, 443 Swift tests in 37 suites, native packaging, relay artifact validation, and pinned legacy v0.1.0 tests/build. Strict Swift format lint also passed; coverage reported 93.30% lines, 91.44% functions, and 85.67% regions.
LOGBOOK.md:84:- REGRESSION: The green gate does not enforce the accepted ADR section 3.1 provider dependency/resource row. `Project.swift` generates `ReluxProxyMacTunnel -> ReluxTunnelCore` only; it does not add `ReluxTunnelMacOSAdapter` or a verified relay resource, and the Release provider contains neither adapter/native symbols nor a relay payload. The earlier target log records this as intentionally deferred because of the SwiftPM/Xcode binary-output collision, but the verification task has no accepted ADR exception and therefore cannot claim an exact-graph pass.
LOGBOOK.md:86:- PRIVACY PROCESS: An initial prerequisite check used an unnecessarily broad parent-directory listing, which exposed unrelated local filenames in the automated spawn log. Accepted evidence must use task-scoped existence/version probes only. The persisted spawn log is sanitized before review and the task outcome contains no unrelated local filename or path.
LOGBOOK.md:95:- CI BOOTSTRAP: The macOS pull-request lane installs Mise 2026.3.10 through `jdx/mise-action` pinned to commit `3c2e0cf82a5b2e5249f0d3635a4d83d0ae861518` and verifies the macOS arm64 binary SHA-256 matching the arm64 `macos-15` runner before invoking the repository-owned Make entry point. A contract regression keeps the runner label and checksum paired. Tuist installation remains pinned and owned by that entry point.
LOGBOOK.md:96:- VERIFICATION: `make credential-free-validate LEGACY_ROOT=/Users/iv/Developer/relux-proxy` exits 0 across contract regressions, deterministic generation, unsigned Debug/Release host and provider builds, entitlement/embedding/linkage checks, 443 Swift tests in 37 suites with 25 intentional known issues, Release build, native packaging, relay smoke, and isolated v0.1.0 legacy tests/build. Signing-required and deferred-iOS lanes are explicitly `NOT RUN`.
LOGBOOK.md:98:### 0113 — macOS target implementation is ready for review; signed Gate P0 execution is separate (TASK-260715-uyju7n)
LOGBOOK.md:99:- IMPLEMENTATION: The generated workspace now has a minimal macOS host and one embedded packet-tunnel system extension at `Contents/Library/SystemExtensions/works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel.systemextension`. The host and provider use the r12 identifiers, macOS 15 floor, shared build/protocol version, target-owned plists, and separate Development/Developer ID entitlement files. The provider imports NetworkExtension and implements only empty start/stop plus version-message handling.
LOGBOOK.md:102:- LEGACY CHECK ANOMALY: `make check-legacy` exits 2 against the independently evolving `../relux-proxy` v0.2.0-dirty checkout because that external checkout no longer matches this repository's v0.1.0 byte/default baseline. The same check explicitly passes the task-relevant boundaries: SwiftPM package/target/executable remain `ReluxProxy`, deployment remains macOS 14, and the generated workspace claims none of the legacy-owned paths. This task does not modify or normalize the external checkout.
LOGBOOK.md:103:- BUILD GRAPH: The minimal provider intentionally depends on `ReluxTunnelCore`, not `ReluxTunnelMacOSAdapter`. Adding the adapter exposed an existing SwiftPM/Xcode transitive binary-output collision: both `ReluxLibSSH2` and `CReluxNativeFixture` produce `include/module.modulemap`. Packet and transport implementation is out of this task's scope; the later runtime-integration task owns resolving that collision before adding the adapter dependency.
LOGBOOK.md:108:- DECISION: The human-approved 2026-07-28 M0 selection is recorded as a task-scoped ADR: pinned libssh2 `a34302491c164d53c900fec9b3cbb050ecebe719` plus OpenSSL 3.5.7 and the one allowlisted six-path patch is primary. ReluxNIOSSH remains comparative FAIL/NOT-RUN evidence and receives no further fork work unless a revalidation trigger invalidates libssh2.
LOGBOOK.md:109:- GATES: Every M0 viability row maps evidence for both candidates. libssh2 has no waived red row; ReluxNIOSSH's missing neutral TCP ownership, opaque signer, bounded intake, algorithm reporting, keepalive, and unbuilt adapter rows remain explicit. The four deferred semantics remain unsupported/notReported under `TASK-260728-3cveay`; physical scale, extension memory, soak, and DNS footprint remain M3 gates.
LOGBOOK.md:110:- MEASUREMENT: Five consecutive current-tree, already-built real-OpenSSH M0 lifecycle runs exit 0 in 11.058–11.144 s test time. Whole-command maximum RSS is 71,254,016 B and maximum macOS peak footprint is 17,891,952 B; every lifecycle iteration asserts zero channels, socket, session, automatic tasks, custom allocations, and buffered bytes. This is a controlled harness envelope containing direct-tcpip, not an isolated DNS-open p99 or physical extension budget.
LOGBOOK.md:111:- REAL HOST: A new explicit-opt-in selected-adapter row executes `LibSSH2TransportFactory` against the owner-approved real relux sshd through a privacy-safe local byte-forwarding path. Three consecutive runs exit 0 in 23.171, 22.654, and 21.904 s with host policy before credential lookup, agent-backed Ed25519 auth, two concurrent direct-tcpip channels, long-lived exec, 48 KiB exec/stdin upload, manual client rekey, five cancellations, and exact zero ownership. Negotiation is consistently curve25519-sha256 / ssh-ed25519 / aes256-ctr / hmac-sha2-256; no host, address, account, key path, key material, or remote content is retained.
LOGBOOK.md:116:### 2233 — SSH production privacy gate and cancellation baselines are deterministic (TASK-260715-2d3g5e)
LOGBOOK.md:117:- PRIVACY: A real libssh2/OpenSSH test injects host, user, endpoint, fingerprint, credential, command, path, stream, and payload sentinels, captures public errors, logger and observer events, metric updates, and snapshots, proves each surface is populated, and scans the combined public representation for leaks.
LOGBOOK.md:120:- VERIFICATION: The named conformance suite exits 0 with 25 explicit ReluxNIOSSH unavailable/red rows; full coverage also passes all 442 tests. Affected libssh2 adapter coverage is 83.36% regions, 94.61% functions, and 92.14% lines. Recursive Swift format lint, core boundaries, and diff checks exit 0.
LOGBOOK.md:126:- VERIFICATION: The candidate-neutral suite and all 441 Swift tests pass; 25 known issues are explicit red ReluxNIOSSH rows because no production adapter target exists. Affected adapter coverage is 83.08% regions, 94.61% functions, and 92.11% lines. Format lint, core boundaries, and diff checks exit 0.
LOGBOOK.md:134:- TESTS: The candidate-neutral Swift Testing suite dispatches the same M0, cancellation-scope, and M3-deferred inventory from candidate data. The libssh2 row invokes `LibSSH2TransportFactory` through real OpenSSH/loopback adapter tests; ReluxNIOSSH has no `SSHTransport` adapter target and is represented by explicit known-issue rows rather than a green emulated fixture.
LOGBOOK.md:135:- COVERAGE: Host-before-auth rejection variants, approved algorithms and opaque signing, direct/exec/upload isolation, bounded EAGAIN/backpressure, byte/time/manual/server rekey traffic, keepalive scheduling/failure, 15 cleanup scopes, complete available metrics, privacy-safe errors, resource baselines, and every deferred runtime surface are asserted. Exact M3 ownership remains `TASK-260728-3cveay`.
LOGBOOK.md:136:- VERIFICATION: 434 Swift tests in 37 suites pass with 25 known issues limited to the unavailable ReluxNIOSSH adapter. Focused affected-file coverage is 84.02% regions, 95.11% functions, and 92.56% lines. Recursive Swift format lint, core-boundary validation, `swift build`, and diff checks exit 0.
LOGBOOK.md:141:- REGRESSION: Round-four review proved that an endpoint supervisor started before final provider state persistence could survive a failed prepare while a later teardown reported zero residuals. The same ownership gap applied to macOS sshd, the task Lima VM, and the real-host endpoint session; lifecycle cleanup also stopped at the first teardown exception instead of attempting every prepared row.
LOGBOOK.md:143:- TESTS: Four injected regressions fail on the old implementation and pass after the fix: partial macOS prepare after endpoint start, partial Linux prepare after VM/endpoint start, partial real-host prepare after endpoint start, and a multi-row lifecycle whose first teardown fails. The final 43-test fixture suite passes and a post-suite process scan reports zero task-owned workers.
LOGBOOK.md:144:- VERIFICATION: Two fresh live lifecycles exit 0 with current/fallback macOS, Ubuntu Lima, and real relux rows reachable as non-root, then report four zero-residual teardowns. Independent checks find an empty provider-state tree and no named Lima instance. Combined unit/integration/live trace coverage is 83.7% for `ssh_matrix_fixture.py` and 90.0% for `ssh_matrix_provider.py`. The streamed 5 GiB source/sink exits 0 with exactly 5,368,709,120 bytes and `SHA256:fc01cfd7aebf90ff9491f8556131b6ef575c3e1fa33a0277ba28920bbaee7f54` and retains no payload. All 428 Swift tests in 35 suites, strict Swift format lint, Python compilation/tabnanny, manifest JSON parsing, and `git diff --check` exit 0.
